  "title": "owned, redis, aside, strict",
  "summary": "A shared Redis with a recorded maxmemory and allkeys-lru policy (approximate LRU, and the report says so). Cache-aside: a miss takes a per-key fill lease, double-checks, loads a committed view and publishes it. A read that begins after a write to that key was acknowledged must not return an older value; a violation fails the cell. The owned model supplies a monotonic cache_version to fence and validate against.",
  "risk": "MUST record zero stale-after-ack reads and zero impossible cache values; a single wrong read invalidates the cell for performance conclusions",
